# Implement Dark/Light Theme Support

This plan details how the application will be updated to fully support dark and light themes, specifically across all internal portal and dashboard views, without modifying `PublicPage.jsx` or application logic.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Since this involves sweeping layout changes by migrating hardcoded colors to CSS variables, please review to ensure no specific component overrides are missed.

## Proposed Changes

### Core Context and App Wrapper
- **`src/context/ThemeContext.jsx`**
  - [NEW] Create new Context provider containing `isDark` boolean state and `toggleTheme` behavior, persisting choice to `localStorage` and syncing with `document.body.dataset.theme`.
- **`src/App.jsx`**
  - [MODIFY] Wrap the top-level application component with `<ThemeProvider>` just outside of `<AuthProvider>`.

### Global Styling Updates
- **`src/index.css`**
  - [MODIFY] Insert `[data-theme="light"]` (and `body`) CSS variables for default light mode scheme.
  - [MODIFY] Insert `[data-theme="dark"]` override variables representing the new dark mode aesthetics.

### Shared UI Components
- **`src/components/shared/Sidebar.jsx`**
  - [MODIFY] Import `Sun` and `Moon` icons via `lucide-react`.
  - [MODIFY] Import `useTheme` hook. Add the toggle button element above the logout button, dynamically rendering light/dark mode wording and its icon.
  - [MODIFY] Convert container inline backgrounds (`#FFFFFF`, `#E2E8F0`), active states (`#EFF6FF`, `#2563EB`), and text colors to the newly created CSS variables like `var(--bg-sidebar)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--sidebar-active-bg)` and `var(--sidebar-text)`.
- **`src/components/shared/ConfirmModal.jsx`**
  - [MODIFY] Update hardcoded `#FFFFFF` container backgrounds to `var(--bg-card)` and text to `var(--text-primary)`.
- **`src/components/shared/StatusBadge.jsx`**
  - [MODIFY] Retain specific status colors but ensure base border/card logic (if any) tracks theme.

### Portal Pages and Nested Components
The following files will undergo text and background color variable replacements, ensuring `var(--bg-app)`, `var(--bg-card)`, `var(--border)`, `var(--text-primary)`, and `var(--text-secondary)` are utilized exclusively:
- **`src/pages/AdminDashboard.jsx`**
- **`src/pages/UniversityDashboard.jsx`**
- **`src/components/admin/PendingApplications.jsx`**
- **`src/components/admin/RegisteredUniversities.jsx`**
- **`src/components/university/Dashboard.jsx`**
- **`src/components/university/IssueCertificate.jsx`**
- **`src/components/university/IssuedCertificates.jsx`**

